# Copy to a file OUTSIDE the repository (for example D:/AVA-Data/deploy/stack.env),
# fill in the values and pass it with `docker compose --env-file <that file>`. Never
# commit the filled-in copy: it holds the passwords and the local model paths.
AVA_ARI_PASSWORD=replace-with-at-least-16-letters-or-digits
AVA_DB_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-long-random-password
# Grafana's admin password (profile `monitoring`). Required by the Compose file even
# without that profile, so a monitoring start can never fall back to Grafana's default.
AVA_GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-long-random-password
# Folders on this host, mounted read-only into the live container:
AVA_ONNX_DIR=D:/AVA-Data/exports/your-export-folder
AVA_ONNX_FILE=your-export.onnx
AVA_CARD_DIR=D:/AVA-Data/exports/your-card-folder
AVA_CARD_FILE=model_card.json
AVA_VAD_DIR=D:/AVA-Data/models/silero-vad/6.2.3
# The AntiDeepfake checkpoint folder (model.safetensors and its pinned files), mounted
# read-only into the api container:
AVA_MODEL_ROOT=D:/AVA-Data/models/antideepfake-mms-300m
# Optional (defaults shown): the lab PBX inside the stack, extension 700, 4 threads
# for the live scorer; for the API 2 torch threads, at most 2 CPUs and 3 GB of memory.
# AVA_API_THREADS=2
# AVA_API_CPUS=2
# AVA_API_MEMORY=3g
# AVA_ARI_URL=http://asterisk:8088
# AVA_ARI_USER=ava
# AVA_TAP_EXTENSION=700
# AVA_THREADS=4
# The internal scrape network `metrics` (always created: `live` and `api` join it) and
# live's fixed address on it, where its health endpoint binds. Change the three
# together: the address must be in the subnet and outside the dynamic range.
# AVA_METRICS_SUBNET=10.231.250.0/24
# AVA_METRICS_DYNAMIC_RANGE=10.231.250.128/25
# AVA_LIVE_METRICS_IP=10.231.250.10
# Scoring settings (PRD FR-A9 file plus reload; defaults shown). The folder is mounted
# read-only into live; the file in it is reread every N seconds (1-60) and a valid
# change reaches calls started afterwards. The default is deploy/compose/config, which
# holds the architecture §7.3 defaults; to edit, copy it to a folder of your own, point
# AVA_SCORING_CONFIG_DIR there with an ABSOLUTE path (a relative one resolves against
# deploy/compose, not this file), and replace the file by writing a temporary file in
# that folder and renaming it over the old one. A missing file refuses start-up.
# AVA_SCORING_CONFIG_DIR=./config
# AVA_SCORING_CONFIG_FILE=scoring.json
# AVA_SCORING_CONFIG_WATCH_S=10
# Prometheus retention (profile `monitoring`):
# AVA_PROMETHEUS_RETENTION=15d
# AVA_PROMETHEUS_RETENTION_SIZE=2GB
